"[Sync] Inject dependencies into TabContentsSyncedTabDelegate" (crbugs
540709814, 575846136, not public; no CVE listed yet): a tab's sync delegate
looked up its TaskTabHelper and SupervisedUserNavigationObserver through the
tab, and they were torn down before it; closing a Sad Tab under a child
account made the sync delegate call into the destroyed navigation observer
(use after free). Both are now passed in, so they are created before the sync
delegate and outlive it. chromium/src main commit
92820d1f3177b96d29faf0212e6a9e437461230b, merged on 2026-11-02 to 157
(635285924de96083135b5a7b9f6d82fd2100b3d3, after the 157.0.8103.41 tag). This
is the 157 merge (Android files included), without its tests. Drop it once a
157 tag has it.

